# 2D sheared granular flow with NO THERMOSTAT.  Theta is set by the balance
# of shear heating against inelastic dissipation; restitution is the lever.
# (_ss variant: adds the step-0 thermal kick below; otherwise identical to
#  in.granular_2d_nothermo.)
# of shear heating against inelastic dissipation; restitution is the lever.
#
# WHY: every n in this project was measured with a Langevin thermostat
# imposing Theta, and Tier 0-A showed n depends on the thermostat damping
# time. So n is not protocol-invariant, which undermines every number. A
# Langevin bath is also a physically odd way to agitate a dense granular
# flow -- real flows generate their fluctuations from the shear itself.
#
# This removes the bath entirely. At fixed gdot and Pconf the inertial number
# I is pinned, while Theta settles wherever heating balances dissipation.
# Raising the restitution e dissipates less and runs hotter, so e scans Theta
# at fixed I with no thermostat anywhere.
#
# HOW TO READ THE RESULT. Do not just compare fitted n. Overlay these (Theta,
# mu) points on the thermostatted matched sweep at the SAME mu_g, Pconf and
# gdot (sweep_matched2d, e=0.5). If both protocols trace one mu(Theta) curve,
# the thermostatted measurement is validated and the tdamp dependence is a
# curiosity. If they trace different curves, the paper's central quantity is
# protocol-dependent.
#
# HONEST CAVEAT: this lever is not clean either. The thermostat varies Theta
# through an external bath at fixed contact model; e varies Theta by CHANGING
# the contact model, and e may affect mu directly rather than only through
# Theta. So agreement is strong evidence the protocol is sound, while
# disagreement is ambiguous between "the thermostat distorts things" and "e
# affects mu directly". Agreement is the informative outcome.
#
# RUN LENGTH: with a bath, Theta is imposed within a few damping times. Here
# the fabric AND the heating balance must self-organise, which takes strain of
# order 0.1-1, so these runs are ~3x longer than the thermostatted ones
# (measurement strain 0.25 vs 0.12).
#
# Usage:
#   lmp -in in.granular_2d_nothermo -var datafile data.q -var mu_g 0.3 \
#       -var e_rest 0.9 -var gdot 1.0e-3 -var Pconf 10.0 -var seed 1 \
#       -var label nt_e0.9 -var nequil 150000 -var nmeas 250000

variable datafile index data.granular
variable mu_g     index 0.3
variable gdot     index 1.0e-3
variable Pconf    index 10.0
variable e_rest   index 0.5
variable seed     index 12345
variable label    index nothermo
variable nequil   index 150000
variable nmeas    index 250000

units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      sphere
boundary        p p p
newton          off

read_data       ${datafile}

pair_style      granular
pair_coeff      * * hertz/material 1.0e5 0.3 ${e_rest} tangential mindlin NULL 1.0 ${mu_g} damping tsuji

neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
comm_modify     vel yes

fix             integrate all nve/sphere
fix             damp all viscous 1.0
timestep        0.001
thermo          1000
thermo_style    custom step ke
run             3000
unfix           damp
unfix           integrate
velocity        all set 0.0 0.0 0.0
# A small starting kick, and nothing more. With no bath and the velocities
# zeroed, the temperature fix nph uses is zero at step 0 and LAMMPS refuses to
# start ("Current temperature too close to zero", fix_nh.cpp:764). It killed
# every frictionless cell in the first attempt at this sweep while the
# frictional ones happened to survive, which is exactly the sort of silent,
# cell-dependent failure this project has been bitten by before -- so the kick
# is applied to EVERY run, not only the ones that need it.
#
# 1e-4 is the smallest value that starts (1e-6 does not). That is of order the
# Theta the shear itself generates, so it is NOT negligible at step 0 and its
# irrelevance has to be demonstrated rather than asserted: the run equilibrates
# for a full strain of 1.0 before the measurement window opens, and
# t_kick_check cells re-run one cell at 10x the kick to confirm the steady
# state does not remember it.
variable        t_kick index 1.0e-4
velocity        all create ${t_kick} ${seed} mom yes dist gaussian
reset_timestep  0

change_box      all triclinic
fix             shear all deform 1 xy erate ${gdot} remap v units box

# Bias-corrected temperature: still needed to MEASURE Theta (remove the
# affine streaming velocity), even though nothing is thermostatting it.
compute         tbias all temp/deform
compute         press all pressure tbias

# Integrate with plain NVE -- no langevin. The barostat still holds Pconf so
# that I stays fixed, but without ptemp: there is no setpoint temperature to
# hand it, so it uses the measured (bias-corrected) pressure directly.
fix             integrate2 all nve/sphere
fix             baro all nph/sphere y ${Pconf} ${Pconf} 1.0
fix_modify      baro press press

compute         cont all contact/atom
compute         Zbulk all reduce ave c_cont

variable        P      equal (c_press[1]+c_press[2])/2.0
variable        tau    equal c_press[4]
variable        muI    equal abs(v_tau)/v_P
variable        Theta  equal c_tbias
variable        rmean  equal 0.5
variable        Iiner  equal ${gdot}*2.0*v_rmean/sqrt(v_P)
variable        Zc     equal c_Zbulk

thermo_style    custom step v_P v_tau v_muI c_tbias v_Theta v_Iiner v_Zc
thermo          5000
log             log.${label} append

run             ${nequil}
print           "=== BEGIN MEASUREMENT WINDOW ${label} ==="
run             ${nmeas}
print           "DONE label=${label} mu_g=${mu_g} e_rest=${e_rest} Theta=$(c_tbias) Z=$(c_Zbulk)"
